    verseRef: "Ezekiel 36:26",
    verseText: '"I will give you a new heart and put a new spirit in you; I will remove from you your heart of stone and give you a heart of flesh."',
    founderMsg: `<p>Hello, New Heart community!</p><p>Normally, we greet one another by saying, "How are you?" That is to say, how is your health, how is your family, and how is your work? Has anyone asked you, instead, "How is your heart?" Perhaps that is more appropriate question or greeting for us. For God it is always a matter of the heart.</p><p>When God sent Prophet Samuel to Jesse's house to select the next king of Israel, God established His principle when He said, <em>The LORD does not look at the things people look at. People look at the outward appearance, but the LORD looks at the heart.</em> This is particularly important and relevant because we are a New Heart community.</p><p>God said, <em>I will give you a new heart and put a new spirit in you; I will remove from you your heart of stone and give you a heart of flesh.</em> It is our prayer and confident hope through our precious faith in Jesus our Lord and through His abundant gift of grace that your heart is well, no matter what your particular situation or circumstances might be.</p><p>We praise and thank our Abba Father for sustaining us in the power of the Holy Spirit through each victorious 4th day. God bless you, your family and your labor of love for God's people and His church.</p>`,
    kidsIntro: "From Los Angeles to Korea, God is giving His New Heart to the youngest members of our family. New Heart Kids weekends create space for children to worship, pray, hear the Word, and encounter Jesus while their parents are being renewed.",
